<title>USA: Salomon discloses top global stock picks for '97.</title>
<headline>Salomon discloses top global stock picks for '97.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salomon Brothers said Tuesday it was releasing a list of top global picks for 1997, 119 stocks in the United States, Europe, Asia-Pacific, Japan, Korea and Latin America.</p>
<p>The picks are listed in a 305-page report, &quot;The Best the World Has to Offer: Our Top Global Stock Picks for 1997.&quot;</p>
<p>Among U.S. consumer cyclical stocks, it named General Motors Corp and Federal-Mogul Corp.</p>
<p>Among technology issues, International Business Machines Corp ; Xerox Corp ; First Data Corp ; Cisco Systems Inc ; and America Online Inc.  </p>
<p>Among healthcare, Centocor Inc ; Cardinal Health Inc ; and Rhone-Poulenc Rorer Inc.</p>
<p>Among financials, Citicorp, Wells Fargo and Co; and Charter One Financial Inc.</p>
<p>Among consumer products, Nike Inc, McDonald's Corp, American Brands Inc, and Tupperware Corp.</p>
<p>Among energy stocks, Energen Corp, Sonat Inc; and Mobil Corp.</p>
<p>Among media stocks, Clear Channel Communications Inc, Tribone Co ; and Comcast Corp.</p>
